    {
      "id": "s5",
      "title": "When one service fails",
      "text": "The reporting system times out. A good outcome tool says so plainly: the CRM and the documents came back, revenue didn't. MCP lets a tool report a failure in its reply, so Claude can tell you, not guess a number.",
      "show": [
        "claude",
        "outcome",
        "t1",
        "t2",
        "t3",
        "brief"
      ],
      "connect": [
        "co",
        "o1",
        "o2",
        "o3",
        "ob"
      ],
      "emphasize": [
        "t2",
        "brief"
      ],
      "dim": [
        "t1",
        "t3"
      ],
      "set": {
        "t2": {
          "state": "fail",
          "note": "timed out"
        },
        "brief": {
          "kicker": "the result · partial",
          "body": "- CRM and documents fetched; **reporting unavailable (timeout)**\n- Owner: Sam Lee · renews 15 Nov\n- 12-month revenue: not available\n- Recent files: renewal proposal, meeting notes"
        },
        "claude": {
          "text": "Here's the brief. Revenue is missing: the reporting system timed out. Shall I try again later?",
          "actions": [
            "prepare_account_brief  account: \"Acme\""
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "title": "Thin or outcome?",
      "text": "Thin tools are flexible; outcome tools are dependable and light on the desk. Our design advice, not an MCP rule: offer both, outcome tools for the jobs you repeat, thin ones for everything else.",
      "show": [
        "tradeoff",
        "spec-note"
      ],
      "emphasize": [
        "tradeoff"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "title": "What to ask for",
